MASTER ENGINEERING TASK

CHOICE PROPERTIES — END-TO-END RENTAL APPLICATION AND TENANT JOURNEY AUDIT

1. Project Context

Repository: https://github.com/choice121/Choice

This project contains an existing real-estate platform and rental application workflow, including:

* Public property listings and property-detail pages.
* A multi-step rental application form.
* Primary applicant and additional adult applicant information.
* Co-applicant and guarantor role selection.
* Application-fee calculation and acknowledgement.
* Payment-method preferences and an existing fee-coordination process.
* Application submission and backend validation.
* Application database records and status tracking.
* Application-credit policies.
* Terms, privacy, and consent pages.
* Application confirmation and administrative email notifications.
* Administrative application management.
* Application review and decision workflows.
* Holding-deposit policies and related processes.
* Lease generation, lease review, and electronic-signature workflows.
* Tenant-facing pages and communications.
* Existing customer-support documentation and business policies.
* Existing integrations and application infrastructure.

Treat the actual repository, database schema, deployed configuration, and implemented business workflows as the source of truth for technical investigation.

Do not assume the documentation accurately describes the current implementation. Do not assume the current implementation accurately represents the intended business policy.

The purpose of this project is to reconcile the existing system, identify its defects, and improve it without unnecessarily replacing the architecture or introducing new services.

