PHASE 7 — APPLICATION REVIEW AND DECISIONS

7.1 Review eligibility

Determine exactly when an application becomes eligible for review.

Inspect:

* Required applicant information.
* Additional applicant completion.
* Consent records.
* Fee confirmation.
* Duplicate submissions.
* Property availability.
* Existing application status.
* Administrative requirements.

Do not introduce a new screening service or claim a screening result exists when the current system does not provide one.

Keep the established review process intact while improving its data integrity and communication.

7.2 Admin review experience

Audit the administrative application interface.

Determine whether staff can easily see:

* Applicant and household details.
* Additional applicant and guarantor roles.
* Application completeness.
* Fee obligation.
* Payment status.
* Application-credit status.
* Property details.
* Current application status.
* Missing information.
* Consent completion.
* Communication history.
* Review notes.
* Decision history.
* Holding-deposit status.
* Lease status.
* Outstanding next steps.

The admin interface should distinguish missing information from an explicit negative answer.

Do not require staff to open multiple unrelated pages to understand the current state of one application if a clear summary can be built within the existing architecture.

