7.3 Decision workflow

Audit approval, denial, waitlisting, withdrawal, and closure.

For each decision, establish:

* Who is authorized to make it.
* Whether a reason is required internally.
* Which information is shown to the applicant.
* Whether the status is recorded before the notification is sent.
* Whether the decision is reversible.
* Whether credits are issued.
* Whether the property remains available.
* Whether the applicant can continue with another property.
* Whether the decision affects other household members.
* Whether the action is auditable.

Avoid automatically treating approval as a completed lease or guaranteed possession of the property.

The user-facing wording must accurately describe the actual state.

