8.1 Email content standards

Every message should clearly communicate:

* Why the applicant is receiving the message.
* Which property or application it concerns.
* The current confirmed status.
* Any required action.
* Any applicable amount, if relevant.
* The deadline, if one actually exists.
* What happens next.
* How to contact the team for assistance.

Use short, direct, professional wording.

Avoid:

* Contradictory instructions.
* Excessive marketing language.
* Unexplained internal terminology.
* False urgency.
* Unsupported promises.
* Unsupported approval guarantees.
* Claims that payment was received when it has not been verified.
* Claims that a property is reserved when it is not.
* Claims that a lease is complete when signatures are outstanding.
* Inconsistent refund or credit promises.
* Inconsistent application-processing timelines.

Use the actual business policy and system state to determine the content.

