PHASE 15 — INTEGRATION WITH THE REST OF THE PLATFORM

The application workflow must remain consistent with the rest of the existing platform.

Inspect connections to:

* Property search.
* Property detail pages.
* Property availability.
* Property IDs and unit IDs.
* Customer inquiry management.
* Property selection.
* Application links.
* Admin dashboard.
* Application status tracking.
* Email communications.
* Tenant account access.
* Lease generation.
* Electronic signatures.
* Move-in records.
* Existing support documentation.

Determine whether an application can be started for:

* A property that no longer exists.
* An unpublished property.
* An unavailable property.
* A property with an incorrect price.
* A unit that is no longer available.
* A property that has been changed since the applicant opened the form.

Check whether changing a property record unintentionally changes an already-submitted application’s historical details.

Preserve the distinction between:

* Current property information.
* The property information associated with an existing application.
* The final agreed lease terms.

Do not let an unrelated listing update silently alter a pending application or signed lease.

