NON-NEGOTIABLE ENGINEERING RULES

1. Inspect the actual repository before proposing code changes.
2. Do not introduce screening services or new screening-provider integrations.
3. Do not introduce payment services or new payment-provider integrations.
4. Preserve the existing fee-collection and confirmation workflow.
5. The intended application fee remains $50 per applicable adult applicant unless explicitly changed by the business owner.
6. Treat the intended application-credit validity as 30 days; investigate and reconcile the repository’s conflicting 45-day policy.
7. Do not silently decide how credits apply to a multi-applicant household. Identify the ambiguity and request a business decision.
8. Do not trust browser-submitted fee totals or status values.
9. Do not mark fees paid without authorized confirmation.
10. Do not issue duplicate credits or consume a credit more than once.
11. Do not send an email that claims an unconfirmed action succeeded.
12. Do not treat application approval as a completed lease or guaranteed possession.
13. Do not treat a holding deposit as an additional charge when the applicable policy says it is credited toward move-in costs.
